Troubleshoot and fix a Docker port mapping issue where the application is unreachable on the mapped host port.

Requirements:
- Located in `/app`, you will find a `Dockerfile` and `app.py`.
- Build the image (`docker build -t myapp:latest /app`) and run a container mapping port 8080 to container port 3000 (`docker run -d -p 8080:3000 --name web_app myapp:latest`).
- Notice that `curl http://localhost:8080` fails with a connection error even though `docker ps` shows the container is running.
- Diagnose why the application is unreachable externally (e.g. testing with `docker exec web_app curl http://127.0.0.1:3000`).
- Fix `app.py` so that the web framework binds to `0.0.0.0` (all network interfaces) instead of `127.0.0.1`.
- Rebuild the image (`docker build -t myapp:latest /app`) and run the container (`docker run -d -p 8080:3000 --name web_app myapp:latest`).
- Ensure `curl http://localhost:8080` successfully returns HTTP 200 OK.
